  "26.1": {
    "title": "Conservative grid and circle contacts",
    "contract": "Input: circles as [integer_id, x, y, radius] and positive cell_size. IDs are unique; radii are positive. At most 512 circles and 4096 occupied cells per circle. Return sorted canonical candidate pairs and sorted true contact pairs. Closed-set touching counts as contact. Reject non-finite data and excessive cell coverage before populating the grid.",
